# Yarr safety

## Read-only default

When media-fleet craft is authorized, these are fine without a mutate verb:

| Surface | Safe actions / tools |
| --- | --- |
| Any service | `service_status`, `help`, `api_get`, `snippet_list`, read-only `op` when the op is clearly get/list |
| Tautulli | `stats_activity`, `stats_history`, `stats_users`, `stats_libraries` |
| qBit | `download_queue` |

Do **not** do the following unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn
naming the title, id, hash, request, or clear create/approve intent:

| Mutate class | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP writes | `api_post`, `api_put`, `api_delete` on any yarr tool |
| Snippet mutates | `snippet_save`, `snippet_run`, `snippet_delete` |
| qBit download mutates | `download_add`, `download_pause`, `download_resume`, `download_remove` |
| File delete | any call with `delete_files=true` / media file purge |
| Tautulli cache | `stats_refresh_libraries`, `stats_refresh_users`, `stats_delete_image_cache` |
| Seerr decisions | approve / decline / delete request |
| *arr destructive | delete series/movie, wipe files, change quality profile / root folder |

Bare product name ("Sonarr", "Plex", "yarr") alone is **not** mutate
authorization.

## Irreversible — confirm blast radius

Before proceeding when clearly authorized:

| Action | State risk |
| --- | --- |
| Library item delete + files | Permanent media loss on disk |
| `download_remove` + `delete_files` | Removes torrent data |
| Bulk queue purge | Many downloads lost at once |
| Quality profile / root folder change | Affects future grabs fleet-wide |
| Mass Seerr deny | Blocks many user requests |
| `stats_delete_image_cache` | Clears Tautulli image cache |

State the object (title/id/hash) and consequence in one sentence, then act
only if authorization already covers that loss.

## Defaults

1. Prefer read/search (`service_status`, `api_get`, `download_queue`,
   Tautulli stats) over writes.
2. Prefer one named item over bulk; require bulk language for bulk acts.
3. Prefer remove-without-files when unlinking a torrent is enough.
4. Prefer MCP tools discovered on the live yarr MCP (`user-mcp_yarr`); do
   not invent tool or action names.
5. Never invent series/movie/request ids or torrent hashes.
6. Site library classification overlays stay in private `homelab` — do not
   hard-code site paths in this portable plugin.
7. Do not paste API keys, cookies, or credentials from tool output into
   chat.

